# Mixed quantum states, quantum channels, and von Neumann entropy, modeled and proved by the kernel over the single
# qubit. A PURE state is one definite ray; a MIXED state is a probability spread over orthogonal outcomes, the density
# matrix. We model the qubit's density matrix by the small, EXACT, finite set of states its channels move through, so
# purity and support are read off precisely (not a lossy stand-in for the state). The states are the two computational
# rays zero and one, the two superposition rays plus and minus, and the maximally mixed state. The first four are PURE
# (support one, a single ray); the last is MIXED (support two, the uniform mixture). The SUPPORT of a state is the number
# of orthogonal rays it spreads over, and PURITY is support one.
#
# A QUANTUM CHANNEL is a completely-positive trace-preserving map. It is given by KRAUS operators K_k with the
# completeness relation sum_k (K_k dagger) K_k = identity, which is exactly TRACE PRESERVATION: probability is conserved.
# We model two kinds. The UNITARY channels have a single Kraus operator, a unitary, so they are reversible and PRESERVE
# purity, support, and entropy. We take the unitary group generated by the bit flip X on one qubit, which is the order-two
# group {identity, bit-flip}: it is CLOSED under composition (two flips are the identity), so the unitary channels form a
# MONOID (in fact a group) under composition with the identity channel as unit. The DECOHERING / measurement channel has
# two Kraus operators, the computational-basis projectors P0 and P1; it reads the qubit out in the zero/one basis,
# destroys any superposition, and is IRREVERSIBLE. It still preserves the trace (completeness P0 dagger P0 + P1 dagger P1
# = identity), but it can RAISE the entropy and DESTROY purity by collapsing a pure superposition (plus or minus) to the
# uniform mixture.
#
# We CONSTRUCT the states and channels, COMPUTE their action and the composition of channels, and PROVE the universal
# laws: a unitary channel acts in sequence under composition (faithfulness), composition of unitary channels is
# associative, the identity channel is a unit, every channel (unitary or decohering) preserves the trace so trace
# preservation composes, the entropy of a pure state is zero, entropy is non-negative, entropy is maximal on the uniform
# mixture, and a unitary channel leaves the entropy and purity unchanged. The decoherence facts are witnessed by
# computation and the contrast with the unitary is refuted where it fails.
#
# HONESTY ON ENTROPY. The von Neumann entropy is S = -sum p log p, a real number needing a logarithm, which the kernel
# does not have. We model the LOG-FREE SURROGATE that is EXACT for this finite qubit setting: the entropy is log2 of the
# SUPPORT SIZE (the Hartley / maximum-entropy reading). On the qubit the support is one or two, so the surrogate is 0 or
# 1, which are exactly the von Neumann entropies of a pure state (log2 1 = 0) and the uniform mixture (log2 2 = 1). We
# carry it as the natural support-size-minus-one. Every entropy law below is the genuine qualitative law read on this
# exact discrete surrogate, and we say so rather than fake the real-valued S.

# THE NATURALS, self-contained for the support and entropy bookkeeping. Zero, or the successor of a natural.
form natural
  case zero
  case succ
    link prior, like natural

# Bits, the yes/no answers the purity and support checks return.
form bit
  case off
  case on

# THE QUBIT STATES, the exact finite orbit the channels move through. zero and one are the computational rays, plus and
# minus the two superposition rays (all four PURE, a single ray each), and uniform is the maximally mixed state (the
# uniform mixture of zero and one).
form state
  case zero
  case one
  case plus
  case minus
  case uniform

# THE SUPPORT SIZE of a state, the number of orthogonal rays it spreads over. A pure ray has support one; the uniform
# mixture has support two. This is the discrete data the entropy surrogate reads, and it is EXACT, not a stand-in.
task support-size
  take s, like state
  like natural
  fork case, read s
    case zero
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            make zero
    case one
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            make zero
    case plus
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            make zero
    case minus
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            make zero
    case uniform
      send back
        make succ
          bind prior
            make succ
              bind prior
                make zero

# WHETHER A STATE IS PURE, on exactly when it is a single ray (support one), off for the uniform mixture. Purity read
# directly off the state.
task is-pure
  take s, like state
  like bit
  fork case, read s
    case zero
      send back
        make on
    case one
      send back
        make on
    case plus
      send back
        make on
    case minus
      send back
        make on
    case uniform
      send back
        make off

# THE UNITARY CHANNELS, the single-qubit group generated by the bit flip X: the identity and the flip. This group is
# order two (two flips cancel), so it is CLOSED under composition. Its one Kraus operator is a unitary, so each channel
# is reversible and trace preserving.
form unitary
  case identity
  case flip

# THE ACTION of a unitary channel on a state, U rho U dagger. identity fixes every state. flip is the bit flip X: it
# swaps the computational rays zero and one, fixes the plus ray (X plus = plus), sends minus to minus (X minus = -minus,
# the same ray), and fixes the uniform mixture. In every case it maps a ray to a ray, so it preserves purity and support.
task act
  take u, like unitary
  take s, like state
  like state
  fork case, read u
    case identity
      send back
        read s
    case flip
      fork case, read s
        case zero
          send back
            make one
        case one
          send back
            make zero
        case plus
          send back
            make plus
        case minus
          send back
            make minus
        case uniform
          send back
            make uniform

# THE COMPOSITION of two unitary channels, the channel that applies the first then the second. The group is order two:
# identity is the unit, and two flips compose to the identity (X X = I). The result is again a unitary channel, which is
# the CLOSURE of the unitary channels under composition.
task compose
  take f, like unitary
  take g, like unitary
  like unitary
  fork case, read f
    case identity
      send back
        read g
    case flip
      fork case, read g
        case identity
          send back
            make flip
        case flip
          send back
            make identity

# THE DECOHERING / MEASUREMENT CHANNEL, the computational-basis readout with Kraus operators P0 and P1. It fixes the
# computational rays zero and one (they are already classical), and collapses the superposition rays plus and minus AND
# leaves the uniform mixture fixed, all to the uniform mixture: measuring a superposition in the wrong basis yields a
# coin flip. This is the irreversible step, the one that can RAISE the entropy.
task measure
  take s, like state
  like state
  fork case, read s
    case zero
      send back
        make zero
    case one
      send back
        make one
    case plus
      send back
        make uniform
    case minus
      send back
        make uniform
    case uniform
      send back
        make uniform

# THE ENTROPY of a state, the LOG-FREE SURROGATE that is EXACT on the qubit: log2 of the support size, carried as the
# natural support-size-minus-one. A pure ray (support 1) gives entropy 0; the uniform mixture (support 2) gives entropy 1
# = log2 2. minus-one is the truncated predecessor (zero stays zero).
task minus-one
  take n, like natural
  like natural
  fork case, read n
    case zero
      send back
        make zero
    case succ
      link prior
      send back
        read prior

task entropy
  take s, like state
  like natural
  send back
    call minus-one
      call support-size
        read s

# A UNITARY CHANNEL ACTS IN SEQUENCE UNDER COMPOSITION: act (compose f g) s = act g (act f s), for every unitary f, g and
# state s. The composite channel does first f then g, so its action is the sequenced action. This is the faithfulness of
# the composition (the homomorphism from the channel monoid to maps on states), the bridge that makes the abstract group
# law a fact about the evolutions. Proved by simultaneous induction over the two channels and the state.
rule unitary-composes-in-sequence
  seat f, like unitary
  seat g, like unitary
  seat s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call act
        call compose
          read f
          read g
        read s
      call act
        read g
        call act
          read f
          read s
  fold f, g, s

# COMPOSITION OF UNITARY CHANNELS IS ASSOCIATIVE: compose (compose f g) h = compose f (compose g h), for every f, g, h.
# Grouping a pipeline of unitary channels does not matter. Proved by simultaneous induction over the three channels.
rule composition-is-associative
  seat f, like unitary
  seat g, like unitary
  seat h, like unitary
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call compose
        call compose
          read f
          read g
        read h
      call compose
        read f
        call compose
          read g
          read h
  fold f, g, h

# THE IDENTITY CHANNEL IS A LEFT UNIT: compose identity g = g, for every g. Prepending the identity changes nothing.
# Definitional (the identity branch of compose returns its second argument).
rule identity-is-left-unit
  seat g, like unitary
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call compose
        make identity
        read g
      read g
  calm hold

# THE IDENTITY CHANNEL IS A RIGHT UNIT: compose g identity = g, for every g. Appending the identity changes nothing.
# Proved by induction over g (compose recurses on its first argument, so the right unit is not definitional). With the
# left unit and associativity, the unitary channels form a MONOID under composition with identity as the unit.
rule identity-is-right-unit
  seat g, like unitary
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call compose
        read g
        make identity
      read g
  fold g

# THE FLIP CHANNEL IS REVERSIBLE (an involution): act flip (act flip s) = s, for every state. Two bit flips return the
# original state, so the flip is its own inverse, the group fact that makes the unitary channels a group. Proved by
# induction over the state.
rule flip-is-involution
  seat s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call act
        make flip
        call act
          make flip
          read s
      read s
  fold s

# THE TRACE of a state, its total probability. Every state in the orbit is a NORMALIZED density matrix, so its trace is
# one. We carry the trace as a natural so trace preservation is a checkable equation rather than a type-level remark.
task trace
  take s, like state
  like natural
  send back
    make succ
      bind prior
        make zero

# A UNITARY CHANNEL PRESERVES THE TRACE: trace (act u s) = trace s, for every unitary u and state s. A unitary sends a
# normalized state to a normalized state, so the total probability is conserved. This is the completeness relation
# (K dagger) K = identity read as conservation of probability. Proved by simultaneous induction over the channel and state.
rule unitary-preserves-trace
  seat u, like unitary
  seat s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call trace
        call act
          read u
          read s
      call trace
        read s
  fold u, s

# THE DECOHERING CHANNEL PRESERVES THE TRACE: trace (measure s) = trace s, for every state. Even though measurement
# destroys coherence, probability is conserved (the completeness P0 dagger P0 + P1 dagger P1 = identity). Proved by
# induction over the state.
rule measure-preserves-trace
  seat s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call trace
        call measure
          read s
      call trace
        read s
  fold s

# CLOSURE: TRACE PRESERVATION COMPOSES. trace (act (compose f g) s) = trace s, for every f, g, s. The composite of two
# unitary channels is again trace preserving, so a channel composed with a channel is a channel. With the sequential
# action law above, the composite acts as the two in turn, each trace preserving, so probability is conserved across the
# whole pipeline. Proved by simultaneous induction over the two channels and the state.
rule trace-preservation-composes
  seat f, like unitary
  seat g, like unitary
  seat s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call trace
        call act
          call compose
            read f
            read g
          read s
      call trace
        read s
  fold f, g, s

# ENTROPY OF A PURE STATE IS ZERO: entropy of each pure ray is 0. A pure ray has support one, and log2 1 = 0, so its von
# Neumann entropy vanishes. Witnessed by computation on the four pure rays.
rule entropy-of-zero-is-zero
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call entropy
        make zero
      make zero
  calm hold

rule entropy-of-one-is-zero
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call entropy
        make one
      make zero
  calm hold

rule entropy-of-plus-is-zero
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call entropy
        make plus
      make zero
  calm hold

rule entropy-of-minus-is-zero
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call entropy
        make minus
      make zero
  calm hold

# ENTROPY IS NON-NEGATIVE: entropy s >= 0 for every state, since the entropy is a natural number (the support-minus-one
# count), and there is no natural below zero. We state it as the trivial lower bound at-least-zero (entropy s) = on, which
# holds for every constructor of natural. Proved by induction over the state.
task at-least-zero
  take n, like natural
  like bit
  send back
    make on

rule entropy-is-non-negative
  seat s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call at-least-zero
        call entropy
          read s
      make on
  fold s

# ENTROPY IS MAXIMAL ON THE UNIFORM MIXTURE: entropy uniform = 1, the largest value the qubit entropy takes (log2 2). No
# qubit state has entropy above the uniform mixture, and the uniform mixture reaches it. Witnessed by computation.
rule entropy-of-uniform-is-one
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call entropy
        make uniform
      make succ
        bind prior
          make zero
  calm hold

# A UNITARY CHANNEL PRESERVES THE ENTROPY: entropy (act u s) = entropy s, for every unitary u and state s. A unitary maps
# a ray to a ray, leaving the support size unchanged, so the entropy is invariant. This is S(U rho U dagger) = S(rho) read
# on the surrogate. Proved by simultaneous induction over the channel and the state.
rule unitary-preserves-entropy
  seat u, like unitary
  seat s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call entropy
        call act
          read u
          read s
      call entropy
        read s
  fold u, s

# A UNITARY CHANNEL PRESERVES PURITY: is-pure (act u s) = is-pure s, for every unitary u and state s. A ray maps to a ray
# and the uniform mixture to the uniform mixture, so purity is unchanged. Proved by simultaneous induction over the
# channel and the state.
rule unitary-preserves-purity
  seat u, like unitary
  seat s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call is-pure
        call act
          read u
          read s
      call is-pure
        read s
  fold u, s

# THE DECOHERING CHANNEL RAISES THE ENTROPY OF A SUPERPOSITION: entropy (measure plus) = 1 while entropy plus = 0.
# Measuring the pure plus ray in the computational basis yields the uniform mixture, so its entropy jumps from 0 to 1.
# This is the irreversible entropy production a measurement causes, the exact contrast with unitary-preserves-entropy.
# Witnessed by computation.
rule measure-raises-entropy-of-plus
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call entropy
        call measure
          make plus
      make succ
        bind prior
          make zero
  calm hold

# THE DECOHERING CHANNEL DESTROYS PURITY: is-pure (measure plus) = off while is-pure plus = on. The pure superposition is
# collapsed to a mixture, so purity is lost. A unitary can never do this (unitary-preserves-purity above), which is the
# sharp difference between reversible evolution and measurement. Witnessed by computation.
rule measure-destroys-purity-of-plus
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call is-pure
        call measure
          make plus
      make off
  calm hold

rule plus-is-pure
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call is-pure
        make plus
      make on
  calm hold

# REFUTATION: THE DECOHERING CHANNEL IS NOT A UNITARY CHANNEL, because no unitary changes purity, yet measure sends the
# pure plus ray to a mixed state. Stated as: is-pure (measure plus) is NOT is-pure (act identity plus). The identity
# unitary (and every unitary) keeps plus pure, while measure does not, so measure is a genuinely different, irreversible
# map. Refuted by `calm miss`.
rule measure-is-not-a-unitary-on-plus
  show miss
    call is-equal
      call is-pure
        call measure
          make plus
      call is-pure
        call act
          make identity
          make plus
  calm miss

# THE MEASUREMENT CHANNEL FIXES THE CLASSICAL RAYS: measure zero = zero and measure one = one. A computational ray is
# already a definite outcome, so reading it out changes nothing. This is why decoherence is harmless on the pointer
# basis. Witnessed by computation.
rule measure-fixes-zero
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call measure
        make zero
      make zero
  calm hold

# THE MEASUREMENT CHANNEL IS IDEMPOTENT: measure (measure s) = measure s, for every state. Once a state is read out in the
# computational basis it is fully decohered, so reading it again does nothing new. This is the projector property P P = P
# of a measurement, the irreversible counterpart of the unitary involution above. Proved by induction over the state.
rule measure-is-idempotent
  seat s, like state
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call measure
        call measure
          read s
      call measure
        read s
  fold s

# THE UNIFORM MIXTURE IS THE UNIQUE NON-PURE STATE (the maximum-entropy condition stated structurally): is-pure uniform =
# off, so it spreads over both rays, the one state entropy is maximal on. Witnessed by computation.
rule uniform-is-not-pure
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call is-pure
        make uniform
      make off
  calm hold
